flowchart TB
    accTitle: Identity verification and MISP authorization are separate stages
    accDescr: A configured login mechanism verifies identity and resolves a local MISP account. Role checks and resource visibility then decide the permitted result; an external identity assertion does not grant access to every record.
    subgraph Identity["Establish identity"]
        direction LR
        A["Verify the configured identity<br/>Password · directory · IdP · front end"] --> B["Resolve the MISP account<br/>Organisation · role · account state"]
    end
    subgraph Access["Authorize the request"]
        direction LR
        C["Check operation and record<br/>ACL · ownership · distribution"] --> D["Return the permitted result<br/>Resource scope · key restrictions"]
    end
    Identity --> Access
